-- title:
--   Prescribing a unit of D⊗mathbb A_f at one place
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring that is a finite-dimensional $\mathbb Q$-algebra, and let $\Lambda \subseteq D$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule that is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb Q$-span is all of $D$. Fix a height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb Q$, i.e. a finite place, and write $\mathrm{ev}_w$ for the $\mathbb Q$-algebra map [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt D w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36), $D \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_f \to D \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_w$, obtained by tensoring the identity of $D$ with evaluation at $w$ on the finite adele ring. Let $y, y_i \in D \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ satisfy $y y_i = 1$ and $y_i y = 1$, and let $g$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_f$ such that for every finite place $w \neq v$ both $\mathrm{ev}_w(g)$ and $\mathrm{ev}_w(g^{-1})$ lie in [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\, w$, the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_w$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the completion at $w$. Then there exists a unit $h$ of $D \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_f$ with $\mathrm{ev}_v(h) = y$, $\mathrm{ev}_v(h^{-1}) = y_i$, and, for every finite place $w \neq v$, $\mathrm{ev}_w(h) = \mathrm{ev}_w(g)$ and $\mathrm{ev}_w(h^{-1}) = \mathrm{ev}_w(g^{-1})$.
--
--   This is the standard device for modifying a finite idele of a finite-dimensional $\mathbb Q$-algebra at a single place while keeping all other components, stated for the lattice-integrality condition given by the local boxes of $\Lambda$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd coset-graph constructions, for instance to produce units of prescribed reduced norm with controlled local components and to prove finiteness of vertex quotients and of stabilisers for the away-from-$v$ unit group.
